{
  "module": "Training: how the numbers are learned",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "pretrain-posttrain",
    "title": "Pretraining and post-training",
    "summary": "The two stages a language model is trained in: pretraining on next-token prediction over a very large corpus, then post-training on instruction data and preferences, with the architecture unchanged.",
    "covers": ["pretrain-vs-posttrain"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "next-token-loss",
        "reason": "Pretraining is defined as minimising the next-token loss."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "training-basics",
        "reason": "Both stages are training, so what training is must already be clear."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "two-stages",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A large language model is not trained in one go. It is trained in "
            },
            {
              "text": "two stages",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", one after the other: "
            },
            {
              "text": "pretraining",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", then "
            },
            {
              "text": "post-training",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Both are training in the sense of the last lessons: adjust the parameters to lower a loss. What differs is the data and the objective."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 74, 80)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "pretraining",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Pretraining",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is next-token prediction over a very large body of text. The loss is the one you have just seen, averaged over enormous amounts of text."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "This is the stage that builds the model's knowledge of language and of the world."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 74)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "posttraining",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Post-training",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " starts from the pretrained model and continues training it with different data and goals:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "first, supervised fine-tuning on instruction and response examples"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "then preference or reinforcement-based tuning, such as RLHF or DPO"
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 74)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "same-network",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Between the two stages the "
            },
            {
              "text": "transformer architecture is unchanged",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". It is the same network with the same shapes. Only the data and the objective differ, and so the parameter values end up different."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 74)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What is pretraining?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Next-token prediction over a very large corpus, which builds the model's language and world knowledge"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It is the first stage of training."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Fine-tuning on instruction and response examples"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is the first part of post-training."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Tuning from human preferences with RLHF or DPO"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That comes in post-training, after pretraining."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Choosing the tokenizer's vocabulary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is done beforehand and is not what pretraining means."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["pretraining"],
      "covers": ["pretrain-vs-posttrain"],
      "variants": [
